From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] Look for Security.framework on Apple's embedded platforms too

libgit2 auto-selects its HTTPS backend, and prefers SecureTransport when
Security.framework is present -- but it only looks for the framework when
CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME is "Darwin".  A cmake iOS cross-build sets that to "iOS",
so the search never runs, SECURITY_FOUND stays false, and the selection
falls through to whatever else is around (mbedTLS, in Julia's build).

That matters beyond which library is linked: SecureTransport validates
against the operating system's trust store, while mbedTLS needs a CA bundle
handed to it, and NetworkOptions deliberately supplies none on Apple
platforms because it expects the system store to be in use.  The result is
an HTTPS backend with no roots configured at all.

--- a/cmake/SelectHTTPSBackend.cmake
+++ b/cmake/SelectHTTPSBackend.cmake
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@
 # We try to find any packages our backends might use
 find_package(OpenSSL)
 find_package(mbedTLS)
-if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Darwin")
+if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Darwin|iOS|tvOS|watchOS|visionOS")
 	find_package(Security)
 	find_package(CoreFoundation)
 endif()
